  "notes": "FarmCore (Assets/Scripts/FarmCore): field farming and irrigation. Packs in Resources/Data/FarmCore load in file-name order; later packs add or replace entries by id. crops: yieldT = fresh t/ha at 100% (Najd centre-pivot wheat 6-7 t/ha, potato 30-40, onion 35-45, watermelon 35-45, alfalfa ~12 t/ha fresh per cut, sorghum 4-6, millet 2-3, open-field tomato 50-70), growDays = in-game days from sowing to ripe at optimum temperature, harvestDays = days a ripe crop stays harvestable before it withers (Settings > Withering), seedBagHa = area one seed bag sows, cuts / regrowFrom = multi-cut forage, forage = mower + baler instead of the combine, rows = row crop. Agronomy (n/p/k need kg/ha, rn/rp/rk removal at 100% yield, fix = legume N, pH range, ecT/ecS = Maas-Hoffman salt threshold dS/m and % loss per dS/m, cardinal temperatures, et = seasonal crop water use mm, ky = FAO-33 yield response to water, residue = straw left) ported from soil.json (FAO-56, FAO-29, FAO-33, Saudi MEWA / Egyptian MALR fertiliser guides). regions: temp / et0 per season (spring, summer, autumn, winter), rainMm per rainy day, capacityMm = plant-available water of the root zone at field capacity (sandy Najd soil ~70 mm, Delta clay ~140 mm), ecWater = irrigation water salinity, gw* = aquifer: start depth m, well limits, metres of drawdown per m3 pumped, recharge m/day in winter and rainy days (Saq aquifer under Qassim falls 2-3 m a year), canal = canal water turns (nobat el-mayya). emitters: eff = share of the water that reaches the roots, salt = salt left behind per mm, evapDay / evapNight = spray and surface losses by day and night (night watering loses less), flowHa = design flow m3/h per hectare covered, headM = pressure head the pump must lift on top of the groundwater depth. pipes: carrying capacity by diameter (PE pipe, ~1.5 m/s). amendments: bagHa = area one bag covers.",
